  "result": {
    "summary": "Matched eight-root arms completed 16 training roots and 32,768 evaluation hands. Training at scale0.01 reduced greedy disagreement to 0.73-1.95% and improved the Standard10 point from scale1 -206.6846 to +1.2207 bb/100, but only 2/4 anchors were positive; uniform was -106.4907 and min-bet -88.6577 with a wholly negative CI.",
    "conclusion": "Preservation-scale training can retain Standard10 and avoid scale1 collapse, but its broad direction is seed/root sensitive and fails generalization. The preregistered 3/4 anchor gate failed, so no larger CFR allocation or Slumbot gate is justified.",
    "decision": "REJECT_STANDARD10_RESIDUAL_REGRET_ROUTE",
    "next_step": "Close residual-regret and from-zero Deep CFR routes. Reassess qualitatively different learned-weight approaches using direct external-transfer evidence rather than weak generic anchors; do not revive single-teacher imitation or local preservation patches."
  },
